The node_list array size must match node_cnt. uint16_t *tasks;
 uint32_t node_cnt;
 uint32_t task_cnt; In the tasks array, each element is the number of tasks assigned to the corresponding node, to its size must match node_cnt. Moreover task_cnt represents the sum of tasks registered in tasks.

uint32_t **tids;
tids is an array of length node_cnt of task ID arrays. Each subarray is designated by the corresponding value in the tasks array, so tasks, tids and task_cnt must be set to match this layout. slurm_step_launch_params_t Data Structure 
 uint32_t envc;
